      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you put a bit more detail as to why FP_RST_ODL is 0, instead of  the state defined in the gpio_rw.inc?\n\nMaybe something like:\n\nAfter EC reboot, FP_RST_ODL is set to 0, so the FP sensor is held in reset. This is because the gpio is only defined in RW. The gpio_pre_init sequence in RW incorrectly ignores setting the init value (from gpio_rw.inc) for FP_RST_ODL because it assumes that the boot is \"warm\", meaning that RO already set the output value.\n\nSee https://github.com/coreboot/chrome-ec/blob/c903c31711f3b2f4370a599b251a61586b3c066e/chip/stm32/gpio.c#L53-L58 .",
      "revId": "6e1ac9ecd5824e8947297c8a9d692c450c856587",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
